Hang on a minute.  "Size" is being used in two contexts in this thread.  There is individual body size (perhaps serving as a surrogate of species, under the assumption that detectability is a function of body size rather than behaviour).  There is group size (number of individuals in a detected cluster) that may influence detectability (under the assumption that larger groups are more easily detected than small groups at large distances).

